{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed bug! Long-press Spanish → \"Browse cards\" opened the card browser with the previous browser-state deck \"French\" (3 cards shown), instead of the requested Spanish deck. Expected \"Spanish\" | \"4 cards shown\". This is the changed feature bug: browser state deck overriding launching screen's request, so browsing a specific deck shows the wrong deck.\n\nI should reproduce once (done: first browse from Spanish when state was All decks → showed Spanish—wait, that first test showed Spanish correctly! Hmm, why?). Let me re-examine.\n\nFirst time: browser state was \"All decks\" (I selected All decks, then exited). Then long-press Spanish → Browse cards → showed Spanish (4 cards). So request won over state All decks? Hmm, or maybe \"All decks\" state isn't \"a deck\" so the request applied.\n\nSecond time: browser state French; request Spanish → French shown. So bug occurs when browser state is a specific deck? Hmm, or maybe the first time the state hadn't been persisted? Actually after selecting All decks, maybe browser state wasn't saved because I exited immediately? No, I did press back. Hmm.\n\nWait, actually first test: I had opened the deck dropdown and selected \"All decks\", then long-pressed comer, selected mesa, opened tags dialog, cancelled, pressed BACK, pressed BACK to deck list. So state = All decks. Then long press Spanish → Browse cards → showed Spanish 4 cards. Correct.\n\nSecond: set French, exit, browse Spanish → French. Bug.\n\nSo maybe bug depends: browser state deck ID persisted; the launching request is applied only if... Hmm. Maybe the initial browser launch (from drawer) had no deck request, so state used. When browsing Spanish the first time, the browser process still existed with state? Hmm.\n\nActually, let me think about AnkiDroid implementation: CardBrowserActivity has `mInitialDeckId` or similar; onCreate loads state. The change \"its starting deck is now loaded from browser state ahead of the launching screen's request\" suggests the code now: load browser state (which sets deckId), then apply request. But if request applied after, request wins. The observed bug means request lost. But why did first test work? Maybe because after using \"All decks\", the saved browser state was \"All decks\" and the request Spanish was applied... inconsistent.\n\nHmm, maybe the bug is reversed: the state load happens after request, and the state save happens... In first test, browser state might not have included a deck (since \"All decks\" may be saved as \"no deck\", i.e., deckId=0?), so the requested Spanish stayed. In second, state included French so it overrode Spanish. That matches: when browser state deck filter is \"All decks\", its deckId=0 and loading it doesn't override because code only sets if >0; when state is a specific deck, it overrides.\n\nSo the bug: opening card browser from a deck (\"Browse cards\") opens previously remembered deck instead of the requested one. Good catch. Let me also verify from another route: opening card browser from drawer after using Spanish? E.g., set browser deck to Spanish, browse... Actually the drawer \"Card browser\" should restore last state — that's intended by the change. Let me check drawer route restores French (state) — likely yes.\n\nAlso check: after browsing Spanish and setting filter to Spanish, then browse French deck → should show French. Likely bug shows Spanish. This is consistent.\n\nNow, is this a genuine bug report? Yes: In card browser, launching \"Browse cards\" for Spanish shows French. Expected the browser to open with Spanish. Symptom type wrong_value or wrong_navigation? It's the browser deck dropdown showing wrong value. I'd use \"wrong_value\" with element_ref = element 1? The toolbar contains \"French\" | \"3 cards shown\" — element_ref 1.\n\nBut first let me continue testing and maybe collect more evidence. Let me test again with a different pair to confirm reproducibility: currently in browser showing