bdeck under Spanish via long-press Spanish → \"Create subdeck\", name it e.g. \"Sub\". Then the deck list should show Spanish with an expand/collapse arrow and child Sub. Test collapse, leave, come back, check persisted. Then restore? We could delete the subdeck afterwards to restore data. Deleting a deck with no cards is possible via long-press → Delete deck. We'll clean up.\n\nAlso note: creating a subdeck might make it appear in card browser deck dropdown; fine.\n\nLet me first finish tag tests in browser before touching deck data? Current browser shows Spanish (from the bug). Let's do tag tests.\n\nTag dialog tests:\n1. Select only mesa (untagged) → tags dialog shows \"verb\" unchecked. Cancel.\n2. Select comer only → \"verb\" checked. Cancel.\n3. Select all 4 → \"verb\" checked. Toggle off, confirm → verb removed from all? Wait, if we toggle off verb and confirm on all selected, it removes \"verb\" from comer. That changes data; we'd then need to restore by re-adding. Could do and restore. But the preconditions say no other tags; modifying then restoring is okay. But risk: If we remove tag from comer, we can re-add via tag dialog. That's reversible.\n4. Select comer+mesa, confirm without change → no change (tag remains on comer, not added to mesa? Actually confirm with checked verb should add verb to mesa too!). Hmm—careful. Opening the dialog with union checked, if I press Confirm, it may add \"verb\" to mesa, changing data. To test cancel, use Cancel. For confirm, maybe test add tag \"test\" then remove it from both; that changes tags data but restores.\n\nActually, safer tests:\n- Cancel keeps data (verify comer tagged verb, mesa not via... how to check? The browser doesn't show tags. Could open note editor and view tags. Alternatively, use the tag dialog with specific row selections to see checkbox state.)\n- We can verify tag membership by selecting a single note and opening tags dialog: checked = has tag.\n\nLet's test:\na) Select only mesa → tags dialog: