{"type": "thinking", "text": "Correct: unchecked for mesa.\n\nNow cancel, select comer only, check dialog shows checked. Then cancel (verify no data change by re-opening mesa? hmm cancel shouldn't change).\n\nLet me cancel and change selection: tap Cancel, then tap comer row to add? Currently mesa selected (1). Tap comer row to add selection (comer + mesa). Since both selected, dialog shows checked (already tested). Instead, to get only comer: tap comer row... that would add, not replace. In this browser multi-select, tapping another row adds to selection. To deselect mesa, tap mesa again. Then tap comer. Or just back out of selection and long-press comer.\n\nSimpler: cancel, tap mesa row to deselect (checkbox), then tap comer row... but tapping a row when in selection mode toggles. After deselecting all, mode may exit. Let me: cancel dialog → tap mesa to deselect (now 0 selected, mode exits?) → long-press comer.\n\nActually let's just do: cancel, press BACK to exit selection, long-press comer.\n\nActually, I realize the union feature might have a subtler bug: with selected rows where the tag is present on some but not all, the checkbox is checked (verified). What if only some tags? Only one tag exists. To test more, I'd create a second tag on one card. Let's do: add tag \"mytag\" to comer via note editor or tag dialog, then select comer+mesa, open dialog: both \"verb\" and \"mytag\" should be checked (union). Then maybe uncheck both and confirm → tags removed from both (hypothetically). Hmm, lots of data changes.\n\nAlternatively, the bug might be that the checkbox state uses the intersection: for comer+mesa with only verb: intersection empty → unchecked, but we saw checked, so not that. Maybe the injected bug is elsewhere in the tag dialog, e.g., after toggling check/uncheck all, or with the \"Filter tags\" search. Or maybe the tag dialog is fine.\n\nWait, but we should test the tag dialog with cards from the same note? Each note has one card. Fine.\n\nLet me consider the changed items again. 4 changes; likely 1-2 planted bugs. We found the browser deck bug. The deck collapse persistence might have a bug too (e.g., collapse state not stored, or stored per collection incorrectly, or all decks collapse together). The deck search may have a bug too (we tested it and it seems fine). The tag union seems fine so far.\n\nLet's test tag dialog more:\n- Cancel: check that tags unchanged.\n- Confirm with no changes: does it add tag to untagged selected? That would be expected behavior of a tag dialog (checking verb and confirming adds to all selected). Not a bug.\n- \"Check/uncheck all tags\" button: toggles all checkboxes? With one tag.\n- Filter tags: search.\n- Add tag: add a tag and confirm, verify state.\n\nLet me do the \"Add tag\" test: On mesa-only dialog currently open... Actually I might use this to create a second tag for union testing. Hmm. But adding a tag to mesa would break \"mesa untagged\" precondition. I can later remove it. Alternatively, add tag to comer for union test then remove.\n\nPlan for tag tests:\n1. Cancel current dialog (mesa, nothing changed).\n2. Select comer only: long-press comer → tags dialog → verb checked. Cancel.\n3. Select comer+mesa: union check verb checked (already done). Cancel → verify by selecting mesa only again: verb unchecked (proves cancel didn't add verb to mesa).\n4. Test adding a tag: select comer only → tags dialog → Add tag → type \"testtag\" → confirm? How does Add tag work: tap +, dialog with text field and OK/Cancel? Adding a tag in the tag dialog presumably checks/creates it. Then Confirm applies. Verify by reopening tags dialog for comer: testtag checked. Then uncheck testtag and confirm to remove it. Verify back to verb only. That tests tags area and \"add tag\" flow.\n\nAlso test the tag filter in the tag dialog: with only \"verb\" and maybe testtag, type \"x\" → no tags; clear. Not central.\n\nAlso there's a \"Tags\" screen? In AnkiDroid, tags can be managed via card browser's sidebar? Hmm, there's no separate tags manager visible. The drawer doesn't show Tags. So the tags area is mainly the tag dialog and searching/filtering by tag.\n\nLet me also test searching by tag in browser search: e.g., type \"tag:verb\" in the browser search box → should show comer only. This tests consistency of tags data. Good idea later.\n\nLet me proceed. Cancel dialog first."}
