{"type": "thinking", "text": "Data restored: only French and Spanish decks, no subdecks.\n\nNow, remaining features to examine:\n1. Deck list and card browser basics — I should check more: counts, sorting, card browser operations (search, deck dropdown, \"Search all decks\", card selection actions). Area is broad; focus on changed features and common bugs.\n2. Tags — tested union, add tag, filter? Not tested tag filter. \"Filter tags\" within tag dialog: type to filter tags. Let me test that (quick). Also note that the tag dialog is the \"card browser tag dialog\" changed feature.\n\nAlso the card browser deck dropdown from other launch routes: e.g., deck overview \"Select deck\"? Hmm.\n\nThe other changed feature: \"Deck list toolbar: deck search results are now computed as each character is typed.\" I tested the deck picker's filter (in browser deck selection dialog). But is that the \"deck list toolbar\"? Hmm. In AnkiDroid, the deck list screen's toolbar doesn't have a search. But the deck picker dialog does. However, the task says \"Deck list toolbar\", which likely refers to the deck list screen's search functionality. Hmm, maybe the deck list screen has a search accessible via \"More options\"? We saw the overflow: Check, Create backup, Restore from backup, Manage note types, Import, Export. No search.\n\nWait—maybe the deck picker dialog (Select a deck) is called \"deck list\" and its search field \"Filter decks\" is the toolbar. The change \"deck search results are now computed as each character is typed\" matched what I tested: filtering as characters are typed. It behaved correctly.\n\nBut hold on: I should also test the deck search from the main deck list. Let me look again at the deck list toolbar: [0] Open drawer, [1] AnkiDroid title, [2] \"7 cards due\", [3] Sync, [4] More options. Hmm, in some AnkiDroid versions the deck list has a search icon (magnifier) in the app bar. Not here. But maybe tapping the title opens...? Unlikely.\n\nAlternatively, the deck picker dialog is indeed the \"deck list\". Fine.\n\nNow, let me revisit the card browser deck dropdown bug more carefully. The changed feature: \"its starting deck is now loaded from browser state ahead of the launching screen's request.\" Maybe the intended behavior is the opposite of what I assumed: perhaps the request should be applied on top of browser state, but only for some routes. My repro: browse French from deck list → opened Spanish. That's definitely wrong user-visible behavior. The developer confirmed it. Good.\n\nAre there other routes: From deck overview screen, is there a \"Browse\" button? The deck overview had an icon at (762,146) that appeared to be \"Select deck\" and then changed the overview deck to Default... Hmm, that was odd. Let me investigate that button: it might be the \"Card browser\" button! Wait, when I tapped it, the screen showed Default overview and snackbar \"Select Deck undone\". Hmm.\n\nActually, looking back: on the Spanish deck overview, elements were:\n[0] Navigate up\n[1] ImageButton [clickable] @(762,146)  (no desc)\n[2] Custom study\n[3] Deck options\nthen title Spanish, counts, Study.\n\nElement 1 at (762,146) with no description. In AnkiDroid deck overview, there's a \"Browse cards\" icon in the toolbar? Hmm, the deck overview toolbar icons: \"Card browser\"? Actually, AnkiDroid's deck overview (study options) toolbar has an icon for \"Card browser\" (magnifying glass-ish with list) and maybe \"Select deck\". I tapped it and the screen changed to a \"Default\" overview with snackbar \"Select Deck undone\". That suggests the icon was \"Select deck\" (opens deck picker dialog) and somehow the deck selection changed to Default and then an undo action... Hmm, weird. Or maybe my tap landed on a \"Select deck\" icon, which opened a deck picker, and the tap coordinates clicked \"Default\" (since the dialog appeared under my finger?), selecting it. Then the \"Select Deck undone\" snackbar appeared from a separate undo? That doesn't make sense.\n\nWait, maybe element 1 was actually \"Undo\"? No, in deck overview, there's an undo button in the toolbar (circular arrow). Hmm, the icon at (762,146) might be \"Undo\"! In AnkiDroid deck overview, the toolbar has \"Undo\" sometimes? Actually AnkiDroid's deck picker toolbar has an \"Undo\" icon (circular arrow)? Hmm no, the deck picker has sync and overflow; the \"7 cards due\" subtitle etc.\n\nHmm, when I tapped it, the overview switched to Default deck and snackbar \"Select Deck undone\" — that's the snackbar for an undo of \"Select Deck\". So the button is \"Undo\"? And the previous action was \"Select Deck\" (maybe a deck select action happened earlier when I was in browser?). Hmm, actually earlier when I tapped element 1 on the Spanish deck overview, it showed Default overview and snackbar \"Select Deck undone\". That means element 1 was \"Undo\" and undid a \"Select Deck\" action that had switched the study-options screen to Spanish? Wait, but the overview was already Spanish at that time. Hmm, I tapped \"Select deck\" earlier? Let me reconstruct:\n\n- I tapped the Spanish deck's counts_layout → Spanish study options screen (4 new).\n- I tapped element 1 at (762,146) on that screen. Result: \"Default\" study options with 0, snackbar \"Select Deck undone\". So the icon is \"Undo\" and undid the action of selecting the Spanish deck, reverting study options to Default. Then I pressed BACK and saw the deck list (Spanish still 4). Fine, nothing important. Not part of areas.\n\nOK so no other route.\n\nNow, we should test the browser's deck dropdown starting state more: The intended new behavior: when opening the card browser from the drawer normally, it shows the last-used browser deck state. We tested: after setting Spanish and exiting, opening from drawer showed Spanish. Good.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: opening the browser via \"Browse cards\" should override the state. The bug. Should I also test after selecting \"All decks\" state then Browse cards → does it show the requested deck? Earlier first test showed Spanish (request worked) when state was All decks. That's consistent with the bug: state \"All decks\" (deckId=0) doesn't override. So the restored state only overrides when it's a specific deck. Our bug report covers it.\n\nNext: Tag dialog's union feature — tested. But maybe there's a bug in a different aspect: the checkbox state for tags when multiple rows selected with different tags. We tested union: comer(verb,testtag)+mesa(none) → both checked. Correct. What about when tag exists on one row in the same note? Multiple cards for same note impossible here (1 card per note). Fine.\n\nWhat about when selecting cards and the tag dialog opened: the checkboxes reflect union but confirming without changes adds the tag to all selected notes. That's arguably intended (dialog semantics: apply checkboxes to all selected). Fine.\n\nWhat about \"Filter tags\" search within the tag dialog: let me test quickly. Also test that unchecking a tag for a selected note removes it and then the tag disappears from the tag list? Not necessary.\n\nLet me test the tag filter now. Open browser, select comer, Edit tags, tap filter, type \"ver\" (verb remains), type \"x\" (no tags), clear. Might as well.\n\nActually, the \"Filter tags\" behavior is not in the changed list, but tags area is. A bug there could be legitimate. Let me test quickly.\n\nAlso, the tags area includes the tag picker when adding a note? Hmm. \"tags\" likely refers to tag management in card browser. We've covered add tag, check/uncheck, union, cancel, delete unused via DB check. There's also long-press tag → create subtag (we saw \"testtag::\" prefilled). Could test creating a subtag \"verb::sub\"? That would create tag data; then check database cleanup. Hmm, maybe not necessary.\n\nLet me test tag filter within dialog. Open browser (from drawer; state Spanish)."}
