le in newer AnkiDroid: tapping \"Sort Field\" opens a dialog letting you choose which column to manage or sort by? Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the dialog title and options: \"Manage column\" with rows each showing \"Column name | sample value\". Selecting one probably sets that column's field. This is the standard \"Manage column\" dialog where you long-press a column header to choose what field that column displays. The sample values correspond to the first card (agua: question agua, answer water, tags -, ease (new), etc.). So this dialog is \"choose which field to display in this column\" for the column I tapped. It appears in both taps (Deck header and Sort Field header) with the same sample (agua) — because it's for the tapped column's slot. Since each tap opened it, maybe tap vs long press is inverted in this build? That would be a pre-existing behavior though.\n\nHmm, wait: maybe I accidentally used long_press? No, I used tap for both.\n\nLet me cancel and inspect: maybe the header has a click-tap for sorting but a long-press for the dialog; the device tap tool might send a slightly long press? Unlikely; tap is quick.\n\nLet me test tapping \"Due\" header and see. Cancel first."}
