{"type": "thinking", "text": "Back in browser. Data consistent.\n\nNow let's think about the deck list & card browser area for any other planted bug.\n\nPotential edge: The count \"7 cards due\" in deck list header vs browser \"7 cards shown\" (All decks). Consistent.\n\nDeck picker filter in browser — tested thoroughly.\n\nWhat about the deck picker filter's \"Collapse\" arrow and Cancel? Fine.\n\nWhat about the browser's deck dropdown starting deck bug: maybe there's an additional related bug where opening Browse cards for a *child* deck or from a deck's context menu when browser state is same works. Not needed.\n\nLet me also verify the \"Browse cards\" bug from deck overview route? The deck overview doesn't have a browse button (it wasn't there). OK.\n\nAnother important test: after \"Browse cards\" opens the wrong deck, does the browser's search bar show state? Not needed.\n\nLet me think about the injected bug for \"Deck list toolbar: deck search results are now computed as each character is typed.\" Perhaps the bug is that search results only update on the first character and then freeze? We tested s→sp→spa→spanx→span (deletion) and it updated each time. But we typed with delays via tool calls. Maybe the real bug only shows when typing fast (race condition)? Hard to test with type_text (it sends text quickly maybe). The phrase \"computed as each character is typed\" suggests a listenable/TextWatcher change. The bug may be that after typing a character, results are stale due to async? Our tests show correct.\n\nHmm, but wait: maybe the \"deck list toolbar\" is the main deck list screen's search, which might be reachable by tapping the \"menu\" or via a hardware search key? Could the main deck list have a hidden search that appears when tapping \"AnkiDroid\" title? Let me test the title tap and the sync/other icons? Tapping the title is harmless. Let me try tapping title \"AnkiDroid\" (element 1) on deck list. Hmm, could open \"Deck list options\". Unlikely.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the \"deck list\" search is inside the \"deck picker\" accessed by the FAB? No.\n\nLet me check the app's Settings for deck list options? Not relevant.\n\nI think the deck search is the picker filter. We tested it.\n\nNow, are there other obvious bugs in tag dialog union? Let me think about \"each tag's checkbox state is now computed from the union of the chosen rows' tags.\" Our test with comer+mesa: verb checked. But maybe the bug appears when tags are filtered? Or when a tag name matches a prefix? Hmm.\n\nWait—there might be a subtle bug: The union computation might be wrong when multiple selected rows have *different* tags. With only one tag, union=check. If the implementation erroneously used intersection, we'd see unchecked for comer+mesa. It was checked, so not intersection. If implementation used \"first row only\", comer+mesa → checked too (comer first? or the selection order?). Hmm! Selection order: I long-pressed comer then tapped mesa. If the dialog computed from the first chosen row (comer), it would also be checked. To distinguish union from first-row, I need a case where the first row lacks the tag but a later row has it. Earlier I tested mesa first then comer? Let's check: The very first tag test: I long-pressed comer first, then tapped mesa → checked; that's consistent with union or first-row(comer). Later, I tested comer+mesa again (comer first) → checked. Did I ever select a row without the tag first, then a tagged row? Let me review: In the beginning, I long-pressed comer (first) then mesa. So order was tagged first. In the second union test, I long-pressed comer again then mesa. Also tagged first. The mesa-only test gave unchecked. So I haven't tested untagged-first-then-tagged! If the implementation erroneously uses only the first selected row's tags, then selecting mesa first (no tags) then comer (verb) would show verb unchecked → bug (not union).\n\nThis is exactly the kind of subtle planted bug the change could introduce. I need to test selection order: select mesa first, then comer, open tag dialog → expected verb CHECKED per union. Let me do that.\n\nSteps:\n1. In browser (All decks, 7 cards), long-press mesa (row 14) → selection mesa.\n2. Tap comer (row 12) → both selected.\n3. More options → Edit tags → check verb state via screenshot.\n\nLet me do it."}
