be intended: the browser's default filter is deck 1 (Default), which is standard in AnkiDroid? Let me recall: In AnkiDroid 2.16, when you open the card browser for the first time in a collection, the deck dropdown shows \"All decks\"? I'm fairly sure the AnkiDroid card browser opens with \"All decks\" filter by default in recent versions... Hmm, actually no: AnkiDroid's card browser maintains a \"Deck filter\" that defaults to the currently selected deck when launched from a deck, or \"All decks\" when launched from the drawer. Hmm.\n\nBut our first launch from the drawer showed \"Default\" 0 cards, which would be a poor default. If that's the planted bug manifestation... but the changed feature (deck dropdown starting deck from browser state) could cause this: browser state's saved deckId was 1 (Default) from some prior default, so it overrides. Hmm, but on first launch there's no launching request anyway.\n\nActually, hold on. Maybe the browser state initially had \"Default\" because the *first* time I opened the card browser, I came from... the drawer on the deck list. No deck request. So falling back to state default (Deck 1). In stock AnkiDroid, CardBrowser's initial deck filter when launched without a deck request is `ALL_DECKS_ID` (-1) or the last state. Hmm.\n\nThe task says \"its starting deck is now loaded from browser state ahead of the launching screen's request.\" This implies there is always a browser state; on first launch the state might be \"Default\". The bug we found is state overriding request. Whether the initial default should be All decks is separate.\n\nI'll not report it, as I can't be confident. But let me test the behavior after a fresh app data? Can't reset app data without tools.\n\nLet me do a final sanity check of the reported bug's exact current state? The developer already confirmed it; no need.\n\nNow let's consider whether the deck collapse state persistence after *collection sync* is expected; can't test.\n\nOne more potential bug